<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Kalka River</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1223</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalka">Kalka</a> River was fought in 1223 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-azov">Sea of Azov</a>, where a Mongol force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a>, raiding west of the Caspian, routed an army of Rus' princes and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a>. Several princes, including Mstislav of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, were killed. It was the first clash between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and the Rus', fourteen years before the Mongol conquest of Rus'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-kalka-river.jpg" alt="Battle of the Kalka River" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sayf al-Vâhidî. Hérât. Afghanistan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MongolCavalrymen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
